In terms of size, the Tropical Kingbird is approximately 7-8 inches in length, making it smaller than some other kingbirds like the Cassin's Kingbird or the Western Kingbird. It has a relatively small head compared to its body, giving it an alert and agile appearance.

Behaviorally, the Tropical Kingbird is known for its acrobatic flying skills, often seen diving and swooping to catch insects mid-air. They are also territorial birds, defending their nesting areas vigorously against intruders.

The unique identifying traits of the Tropical Kingbird include its bright yellow underparts, grayish-blue upperparts, and dark gray wings and tail. These features make it easily distinguishable from other similar species such as the Yellow-rumped Warbler or the Yellow-bellied Flycatcher.
